<h3>53:09 — Lecture end: synchronized keyword summary</h3>
<p>What you should know after Video 088:</p>
<p>Sir: Is it clear for all of you? — end of Multi Threading Part-8 / synchronization part-2.</p>
<h2>Quick reference — lock cheat sheet</h2>
<pre class='code'>// INSTANCE synchronized method → object lock of &quot;this&quot; (the instance used to call)
void instanceSync() { synchronized (this) { } }  // equivalent lock concept

// STATIC synchronized method → class lock of the declaring class
static synchronized void staticSync() { }

// Same object, two synchronized instance methods → same lock → serialize access
synchronized void m1() { }
synchronized void m2() { }  // blocks on same instance

// Different objects → different locks → no cross-object blocking
Display d1 = new Display();
Display d2 = new Display();  // d1 lock != d2 lock
// OCJP-style: which lock?
class Test {
    static synchronized void a() { }  // Class lock: Test.class
    synchronized void b() { }        // Object lock: this instance
    static void c() { }               // No lock
    void d() { }                      // No lock
}</pre>
