<tr><td>Different objects, multiple threads</td><td>Instance `synchronized` does not block across objects → irregular if they share a resource externally (e.g. console)</td></tr>
<tr><td>`static synchronized`</td><td>Uses class-level lock — one thread per class for all static synchronized methods of that class</td></tr>
<tr><td>Class vs object lock</td><td>Independent — holding one does not block the other</td></tr>
<tr><td>Class X / M1–M5</td><td>While static sync runs, normal static + instance methods (non-competing locks) can still run</td></tr>
<tr><td>`displayN` / `displayC`</td><td>Two synchronized methods on same object share one lock → mutual exclusion</td></tr>
<tr><td>Next</td><td>Synchronized block</td></tr>
</table>
<table>
<tr><th>#</th><th>Setup</th><th>Method sync type</th><th>Objects</th><th>Output</th></tr>
<tr><td>1</td><td>wish — recap</td><td>instance synchronized</td><td>1</td><td>Regular</td></tr>
<tr><td>2</td><td>wish — d1, d2</td><td>instance synchronized</td><td>2</td><td>Irregular</td></tr>
<tr><td>3</td><td>wish — d1, d2</td><td>`static synchronized`</td><td>2</td><td>Regular</td></tr>
<tr><td>4</td><td>displayN + displayC</td><td>not synchronized</td><td>1</td><td>Irregular (mixed)</td></tr>
<tr><td>5</td><td>displayN + displayC</td><td>both synchronized</td><td>1</td><td>Regular</td></tr>
</table>
</body></html>
